# TrendVaulta - Cursor AI Rules

## Project Overview
TrendVaulta is a monorepo retail e-commerce platform for beauty, fashion, and lifestyle products. It includes a Next.js storefront, a Vite admin dashboard, and an Express.js API with MongoDB and Stripe.

## Tech Stack
- **Storefront** (`apps/website`): Next.js 16 (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, React Query, Zustand, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion
- **Dashboard** (`apps/dashboard`): Vite + React 19, TypeScript, React Query, Zustand, Tailwind CSS, React Router
- **Backend** (`apps/api`): Express.js, Node.js, MongoDB, Mongoose, Stripe, Nodemailer
- **Shared packages** (`packages/`): `@trendvaulta/types`, `@trendvaulta/api-client`
- **Package Manager**: npm workspaces (root `package.json`)

## Monorepo Structure
```
trendvaulta/
├── apps/
│   ├── api/          # Express.js backend (port 3000)
│   ├── website/      # Next.js storefront (port 3001)
│   └── dashboard/    # Vite admin dashboard (port 3002)
├── packages/
│   ├── types/
│   └── api-client/
└── docs/             # Audits, gap analysis, backlog notes
```

## File Structure
- **Storefront** (`apps/website/src/`):
  - `app/` — Next.js App Router pages
  - `components/` — Reusable UI (including `home/` storefront rails)
  - `components/ui/` — Base UI primitives
  - `lib/` — API client, utilities
  - `hooks/` — React Query hooks by domain
  - `types/` — TypeScript definitions
  - `data/` — Demo/fallback storefront data when APIs are unavailable

- **Dashboard** (`apps/dashboard/src/`):
  - Vite SPA pages/hooks for admin catalog, orders, users, settings

- **Backend** (`apps/api/`):
  - `controllers/` — Route controllers
  - `models/` — Mongoose models
  - `routes/` — Express routes
  - `middlewares/` — Auth, CORS, validation helpers
  - `services/` / `utils/` — Stripe, mail, helpers
  - `seeder.js` + `data.js` — Seed script (see `SEEDER_README.md`)

## API Integration
- Storefront: `apps/website/src/lib/api.ts` (+ domain hooks)
- Dashboard: `apps/dashboard/src/lib/api.ts` and/or `@trendvaulta/api-client`
- Backend routes under `apps/api/routes/`, mounted in `apps/api/app.js`
- JWT via `verfiyToken` middleware (note existing spelling)
- Typical response shape: `{ message, data?, errors? }` (confirm per controller)

## Domain
Primary catalog resources are **products** and **brands**, plus orders, payments, wishlist, reviews, coupons, offers, recommendations, bundles, recently-viewed, gift-finder, lookbooks, and storefront content endpoints.

## Styling
- Match the **existing** storefront/dashboard design system in each app
- Tailwind CSS; Framer Motion where already used
- Mobile-first responsive design
- Do not invent a new visual theme unless the task is explicitly a redesign

## Key Features
- JWT auth (login, register, password reset)
- Product browsing, search, badges, sorting (e.g. bestselling)
- Brands (including featured)
- Cart, wishlist, checkout (Stripe)
- Orders and admin management
- Reviews & ratings
- Coupons / offers
- Storefront rails (deals, recommendations, lookbooks, trust, testimonials, etc.)
- Admin dashboard (products, brands, orders, users, coupons, offers, reviews, stats)

## Code Style
- Functional components with hooks
- TypeScript on website/dashboard
- camelCase variables, PascalCase components
- Async/await
- Small, focused changes matching local patterns

## Git Workflow
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`
- Atomic, focused commits
- Agents: suggest commit message only unless user explicitly asks to commit

## Important Notes
- API default port **3000** (`PORT` env override)
- Website **3001**, dashboard **3002**
- Restart API after adding new routes
- Use React Query for server state
- Arabic-first UX where the project already uses Arabic
- User-facing errors must be safe/localized — never raw stack traces or internal keys
